      "name": "main",
      "text": "Half-wave diode rectifier with RC smoothing, 5 V 50 Hz\n* D1 conducts near the top of each positive half-cycle and charges C1 to about\n* 5 V - 0.7 V. Between peaks R1 discharges C1: ripple ~ Vout / (f R C) = 0.4 V.\n* Plot V(in) and V(out) together to see the conduction angle and the ripple.\nV1 in 0 SIN(0 5 50)\nD1 in out d1n4148\nC1 out 0 100u\nR1 out 0 2.2k\n.model d1n4148 D (is=2.52n n=1.752 rs=0.568 bv=100 ibv=100u cjo=4p)\n.tran 50u 100m\n.end\n"
    }
